{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added `POST /v1/api-keys/{apiKeyID}/regenerate`. New `Storage.RegenerateAPIKey` (internal/storage/api_key.go) replaces the token in a single UPDATE scoped to the key ID and the calling user, so the old token stops authenticating immediately and the new one works. New `regenerateAPIKeyHandler` (internal/api/api_key_handlers.go) is registered in internal/api/api.go and returns 200 with the API key object including the new `token`; 400 for an invalid ID, 404 if the key does not exist or belongs to another user. Regenerating also resets `last_used_at` to null, since the new token has not been used \u2014 a choice not specified in the task. Existing unit and integration tests pass; the new endpoint itself is not exercised by them.", "t": 1794462926.385}
